# Example 11: Protein structure prediction - mixed helix/sheet propensity
# The gene encodes a small ~50 aa protein with alternating alpha-helix / beta-sheet / random-coil segments
#
# Segment design (propensity):
#   alpha-helix  : Ala(GCT) Glu(GAA) Leu(CTG)  - high helix propensity
#   beta-sheet   : Val(GTT) Ile(ATT) Phe(TTT)  - high sheet propensity
#   loop         : Gly(GGT) Ser(TCT)            - flexible turns
#
# HelixLang's ORF provides the protein sequence; the structure report is
# computed through the #sim extension point (kind=protein_structure) with
# the Chou-Fasman-style propensity model of helixlang.protein_structure.

#promoter name=p_fold strength=-0.4

#gene name=folding_demo promoter=p_fold
ATG GCT GAA CTG GCT GAA CTG GCT GAA CTG GGT TCT GGT GTT ATT TTT GTT ATT TTT GGT TCT GGT GCT GAA CTG GCT GAA CTG GGT TCT GGT GTT ATT TTT GTT ATT GGT TCT GCT GAA CTG GCT GAA CTG GCT GGT TCT GGT GTT ATT TTT TAA
#end

#regulate p_fold -> folding_demo strength=+0.8

#config backend=fba ticks=1
#sim kind=protein_structure
